  "chunk": "descending into darkness.\nWhat command should I enter?\nThought process: I’ve opened the trap door from above. Now I should\ngo back down to the studio to retrieve my treasures, bring them up, and\ndeposit them in the trophy case.\n> GO DOWN\nGame output:The trap door crashes shut, and you hear someone bar-\nring it. Cellar\n11\nropic, OpenAI, and Google) failed to improve game progress, suggesting that\nwhat these systems label as “thinking” does not adequately capture the cognitive\nprocesses we associate with human problem-solving.\nQualitative analysis of the models’ behaviour revealed this issue. All models\ndemonstrated limited metacognition—the ability to monitor one’s own thinking\nand recognize when a strategy is failing. They often continued attempting\nunsuccessful actions without adapting their approach, and failed to learn from\nmistakes across multiple game sessions. These patterns point to a fundamental\ndistinction between pattern matching and genuine understanding. The models",
